## Three things worth knowing that are not in any commit message

**The first-run card blocked the UI tests, and would have blocked a user.**
The first version was a full-screen overlay. Every UI test starts on a
fresh data folder, so it opened and intercepted every click; Playwright said
so in as many words. It contradicted the card's own stated rule, and the
fix (`f7b35b4`) moved it into the home screen with no scrim. The tests found
it before a user did.

**Two bugs only real tests caught.** `backup_webhook.url()` called
`vault.get` on the module rather than the instance; the AttributeError was
swallowed by the locked-vault guard, so the webhook would have silently
never fired — found because the test posts to a live HTTP server. And
`start_pull` read the state back after starting the thread, so a fast pull
reported "done" for one the caller never saw begin.

**One flake, found and fixed.** `test_ansible_env_keys.py` failed under the
full suite twice — different assertions each time, which is what a race
looks like — and passed alone both times. Its post-accept waits were fixed
200ms sleeps; they now wait for the list to show the expected text. 23/23
with two other Playwright suites running as load. Test-only, so the
executable built at `654942c` carries every non-test change in the batch.

